---
term: Amendment
section: evolution-and-protection
order: 20
definition: A proposed or adopted change to the text of a charter.
seeAlso:
  - living-charter
  - constitutional-layering
---
Amendments are the main subject of political debate in the Social Charter. Instead of choosing between candidates, members argue about specific articles, objectives, jurisdictions, and arbitration rules. Each amendment follows the procedure that the charter's [[meta-governance]] layer defines, and it must meet the [[amendment threshold]] for the layer it changes.
